WEBVTT

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:22.937
<i>Kristin: hey, meredith, it's kristin.</i>

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:25.137
<i>You have to tell me
what happened last night.</i>

00:03:25.170 --> 00:03:26.137
<i>Call me.</i>

00:03:27.337 --> 00:03:29.471
<i>Brad: hey, meredith. Brad calling.</i>

00:03:29.504 --> 00:03:32.304
<i>Listen, do you want to hook up later?</i>

00:03:32.337 --> 00:03:35.671
<i>Well, i'll talk to you
then. Give me a call. Thanks.</i>

00:03:40.271 --> 00:03:42.738
<i>Brock: hey, meredith, what's
going on? This is brock.</i>

00:03:42.770 --> 00:03:45.571
<i>I just wanted to let you know
the gang is gonna get together.</i>

00:03:45.604 --> 00:03:47.404
<i>We're gonna go to the garage.</i>

00:03:47.437 --> 00:03:49.437
<i>We're gonna have some
beers and some shots.</i>

00:04:19.970 --> 00:04:22.937
All right, dean, this is the place.

00:04:22.970 --> 00:04:24.937
I've got to say dad and me did just fine

00:04:24.970 --> 00:04:27.304
Without these stupid costumes.

00:04:27.337 --> 00:04:30.638
I feel like a
high-School-Drama dork.

00:04:32.504 --> 00:04:34.471
What was that play that you did?

00:04:34.504 --> 00:04:36.304
What was it
-- "Our town"?

00:04:36.337 --> 00:04:37.970
Yeah, you were good. It was cute.

00:04:38.004 --> 00:04:39.803
Look, you want to pull this off or not?

00:04:39.837 --> 00:04:42.337
I'm just saying these outfits
cost hard-Earned money.

00:04:42.371 --> 00:04:43.437
Whose?

00:04:43.471 --> 00:04:46.803
Ours. You think
credit-Card fraud is easy?

00:04:49.070 --> 00:04:51.037
Thanks for letting us look around.

00:04:51.070 --> 00:04:54.571
The police said they were
done with the place, so...

00:05:05.204 --> 00:05:07.337
You guys said you were
with the alarm company?

00:05:07.371 --> 00:05:08.704
That's right.

00:05:08.738 --> 00:05:10.004
Well, no offense,

00:05:10.037 --> 00:05:13.170
But your alarm is about as
useful as boobs on a man.

00:05:13.204 --> 00:05:15.170
Well, that's
why we're here --

00:05:15.204 --> 00:05:18.537
To see what went wrong, to
stop it from happening again.

00:05:20.571 --> 00:05:22.371
Now, ma'am, you found the body?

00:05:22.404 --> 00:05:23.537
Yeah.

00:05:23.571 --> 00:05:24.870
Right after it happened?

00:05:24.903 --> 00:05:26.204
No, a few days later.

00:05:26.237 --> 00:05:28.870
Meredith's work called.
She hadn't showed up.

00:05:28.903 --> 00:05:30.970
I knocked on her door.

00:05:31.004 --> 00:05:33.937
That's when i noticed... the smell.

00:05:33.970 --> 00:05:37.404
Any windows open? Any sign of break-In?

00:05:37.437 --> 00:05:38.870
Windows were locked.
Front door was bolted.

00:05:38.903 --> 00:05:41.271
Chain was on the door. We
had to cut it to get in.

00:05:41.304 --> 00:05:42.604
And the alarm was still on?

00:05:42.638 --> 00:05:45.604
Like i said. Bang-Up job
your company is doing.

00:05:45.638 --> 00:05:47.704
Did you see any overturned furniture,

00:05:47.738 --> 00:05:49.371
Broken glass, signs of struggle?

00:05:49.404 --> 00:05:52.337
Everything was in perfect condition...

00:05:52.371 --> 00:05:54.271
Except meredith.

00:05:54.304 --> 00:05:57.437
Well, what condition was meredith in?

00:05:57.471 --> 00:06:00.837
Meredith was all over, in pieces.

00:06:00.870 --> 00:06:03.704
The guy who killed her
must have been a whack job.

00:06:03.738 --> 00:06:06.304
But i tell you, if i
didn't know any better,

00:06:06.337 --> 00:06:08.537
I'd have said a wild animal did it.

00:06:11.571 --> 00:06:14.170
Ma'am, you mind if we take some time,

00:06:14.204 --> 00:06:16.271
Give this place a once-Over?

00:06:16.304 --> 00:06:19.704
Go right ahead. Knock yourself out.

00:06:25.104 --> 00:06:27.237
So the killer walks in
and out of the apartment --

00:06:27.271 --> 00:06:28.738
No weapons, no prints, nothing.

00:06:28.770 --> 00:06:31.070
I'm telling you, the
minute i found that article,

00:06:31.104 --> 00:06:32.738
I knew this was our kind of gig.

00:06:32.770 --> 00:06:34.271
I think i agree with you.

00:06:34.304 --> 00:06:36.770
So, you talked to the cops?

00:06:36.803 --> 00:06:40.304
Uh, yeah, i
spoke to amy --

00:06:40.337 --> 00:06:44.304
A, uh, charming, perky
officer of the law.

00:06:44.337 --> 00:06:45.638
What did you find out?

00:06:45.671 --> 00:06:48.638
Well, she's a sagittarius.
She loves tequila.

00:06:48.671 --> 00:06:50.837
I mean...whew.

00:06:50.870 --> 00:06:53.004
Oh, and she's got this
little tattoo. Dean!

00:06:53.037 --> 00:06:54.170
What? Yeah.

00:06:54.204 --> 00:06:56.004
Nothing we don't already know,

00:06:56.037 --> 00:06:59.304
Except for one thing they're
keeping out of the papers.

00:06:59.337 --> 00:07:00.770
Meredith's heart was missing.

00:07:02.604 --> 00:07:03.738
Her heart?

00:07:03.770 --> 00:07:06.237
Yeah, her heart.

00:07:06.271 --> 00:07:08.070
So, what do you think did it to her?

00:07:08.104 --> 00:07:10.471
The landlady said it looked
like an animal attack.

00:07:10.504 --> 00:07:13.371
Maybe it was. Werewolf?

00:07:13.404 --> 00:07:15.271
Not a werewolf. The
lunar cycle's not right.

00:07:15.304 --> 00:07:16.337
If it was a creature,

00:07:16.371 --> 00:07:18.137
It would've left some kind of trace.

00:07:18.170 --> 00:07:21.803
It was probably a spirit.

00:07:21.837 --> 00:07:23.937
Hmm.

00:07:23.970 --> 00:07:27.471
See if you can find
any masking tape around.

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:52.371
Ever see that symbol before?

00:07:52.404 --> 00:07:54.837
Never.

00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:56.837
Me, neither.

00:08:30.204 --> 00:08:32.504
I talked to the bartender.

00:08:32.537 --> 00:08:34.937
Did you get anything...
besides her number?

00:08:34.970 --> 00:08:38.803
Dude, i'm a professional.
I'm offended that...

00:08:40.437 --> 00:08:43.037
All right.

00:08:43.070 --> 00:08:45.237
You mind doing a little bit of thinking

00:08:45.271 --> 00:08:47.070
With your upstairs brain, dean?

00:08:47.104 --> 00:08:48.803
Hmm? There's nothing to find out.

00:08:48.837 --> 00:08:50.837
Meredith worked here. She waited tables.

00:08:50.870 --> 00:08:53.371
Everyone here is her friend.
Everyone says she's normal.

00:08:53.404 --> 00:08:55.704
She didn't do or say anything
weird before she died.

00:08:55.738 --> 00:08:57.970
What about that symbol?
Did you find anything?

00:08:58.004 --> 00:08:59.371
Nope. Nothing.

00:08:59.404 --> 00:09:01.870
It wasn't in dad's journal
or in any of the usual books.

00:09:01.903 --> 00:09:04.638
I just have to dig a
little deeper, i guess.

00:09:04.671 --> 00:09:08.037
There was a first victim,
right, before meredith?

00:09:08.070 --> 00:09:10.037
Right, yeah. His name was, uh...

00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:12.070
His name was ben swardstrom.

00:09:12.104 --> 00:09:14.738
Last month he was found
mutilated in his town house.

00:09:14.770 --> 00:09:17.803
Same deal. The door was
locked. The alarm was on.

00:09:17.837 --> 00:09:19.738
Is there any connection between them?

00:09:19.770 --> 00:09:21.070
Nothing i could tell.

00:09:21.104 --> 00:09:23.104
Ben was a banker.
Meredith was a waitress.

00:09:23.137 --> 00:09:25.204
They never met, never
knew anyone in common.

00:09:25.237 --> 00:09:27.571
They were practically
from different worlds.

00:09:27.604 --> 00:09:29.404
So the only successful
intel we've scored

00:09:29.437 --> 00:09:32.104
Is the bartender's phone number.

00:09:33.204 --> 00:09:35.404
What?

00:09:38.437 --> 00:09:39.604
Sam?

00:09:47.970 --> 00:09:49.104
Meg.

00:09:49.137 --> 00:09:50.704
Sam!

00:09:54.970 --> 00:09:59.170
Sam, is that you? Oh, my gosh!

00:10:00.970 --> 00:10:03.970
What are you doing here?

00:10:04.003 --> 00:10:05.937
I'm just in town
-- Visiting friends.

00:10:07.903 --> 00:10:09.037
Where are they?

00:10:09.070 --> 00:10:11.371
Well, they're not here right now,

00:10:11.404 --> 00:10:12.970
But what about you, meg?

00:10:13.003 --> 00:10:14.838
I thought you were going to california.

00:10:14.870 --> 00:10:16.170
Oh, i did.

00:10:16.204 --> 00:10:18.371
I came. I saw. I conquered.

00:10:18.404 --> 00:10:20.903
Oh, and i met
what's his name --

00:10:20.937 --> 00:10:23.404
Something michael
murray -- At a bar.

00:10:23.437 --> 00:10:24.571
Who?

00:10:24.604 --> 00:10:25.838
It doesn't matter.

00:10:25.870 --> 00:10:28.237
Anyway, the whole scene got old,

00:10:28.270 --> 00:10:30.537
So i'm living here for a while.

00:10:31.771 --> 00:10:33.070
You're from chicago?

00:10:33.104 --> 00:10:36.070
No, massachusetts
-- Andover.

00:10:36.104 --> 00:10:37.637
Gosh, sam,

00:10:37.671 --> 00:10:39.838
What are the odds we'd
run into each other?

00:10:39.870 --> 00:10:41.838
I know. I thought i'd
never see you again.

00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:44.104
Well, i'm glad you were wrong.

00:10:47.537 --> 00:10:49.537
Dude, cover your mouth.

00:10:49.571 --> 00:10:52.437
Yeah, i'm sorry, meg.

00:10:52.471 --> 00:10:55.671
This is, um -- This
is my brother, dean.

00:10:57.704 --> 00:10:58.903
This is dean?

00:10:58.937 --> 00:11:00.704
Yeah. So you've heard of me?

00:11:00.738 --> 00:11:02.537
Oh, yeah, i've heard of you.

00:11:02.571 --> 00:11:06.337
Nice -- The way you treat
your brother like luggage.

00:11:06.371 --> 00:11:07.671
Sorry?

00:11:07.704 --> 00:11:10.270
Why don't you let him
do what he wants to do?

00:11:10.304 --> 00:11:12.704
Stop dragging him
over god's green earth.

00:11:12.738 --> 00:11:14.903
Meg...it's all right.

00:11:17.237 --> 00:11:20.371
Okay. Awkward.

00:11:20.404 --> 00:11:23.437
I'm gonna get a drink now.

00:11:28.003 --> 00:11:29.304
Sam, i'm sorry.

00:11:29.337 --> 00:11:34.003
It's just, the way you
told me he treats you,

00:11:34.037 --> 00:11:35.870
If it were me, i'd kill him.

00:11:35.903 --> 00:11:37.404
It's all right. He means well.

00:11:37.437 --> 00:11:40.037
We should hook up while you're in town.

00:11:40.070 --> 00:11:41.204
Yeah.

00:11:41.237 --> 00:11:43.237
I could show you a hell of a time.

00:11:43.270 --> 00:11:44.537
That sounds great.

00:11:44.571 --> 00:11:46.537
Why don't you give me your number?

00:11:46.571 --> 00:11:49.870

312-555-0143.

00:11:49.903 --> 00:11:51.738
You know what? I never
got your last name.

00:11:51.771 --> 00:11:53.371
Masters. Masters?

00:11:53.404 --> 00:11:54.604
So you better call.

00:11:54.637 --> 00:11:56.604
Scout's honor.

00:11:56.637 --> 00:12:00.637
I hope to see you around, sam.

00:12:10.137 --> 00:12:11.437
Who the hell we he?

00:12:11.471 --> 00:12:13.437
I don't really know.
I only met her once.

00:12:13.471 --> 00:12:15.771
Meeting up with her again?

00:12:15.804 --> 00:12:19.104
I don't know, man. It's weird.

00:12:19.137 --> 00:12:21.771
What was she saying --
I treat you like luggage?

00:12:21.804 --> 00:12:23.771
Were you bitching
about me to some chick?

00:12:23.804 --> 00:12:25.104
Look, i'm sorry, dean.

00:12:25.137 --> 00:12:26.604
It was when we had that huge fight

00:12:26.637 --> 00:12:28.637
When i was in the bus stop in indiana.

00:12:28.671 --> 00:12:30.637
Is there any truth to what she's saying?

00:12:30.671 --> 00:12:32.504
Am i keeping you against your will, sam?

00:12:32.537 --> 00:12:34.437
No, of course not.
Now, would you listen?

00:12:34.471 --> 00:12:36.437
What?!

00:12:36.471 --> 00:12:38.937
I think there's something
strange going on here, dean.

00:12:38.970 --> 00:12:40.571
Tell me about it. She
wasn't even into me.

00:12:40.604 --> 00:12:43.137
No, man, i mean, like
our kind of strange.

00:12:43.170 --> 00:12:45.137
Maybe even a lead. Why do you say that?

00:12:45.170 --> 00:12:47.937
I met meg weeks ago literally
on the side of the road.

00:12:47.970 --> 00:12:50.237
Now i run into her in
some random chicago bar --

00:12:50.270 --> 00:12:51.771
The same bar where a waitress

00:12:51.804 --> 00:12:53.838
Was slaughtered by
something supernatural.

00:12:53.870 --> 00:12:55.804
You don't think that's
weird? It happens.

00:12:55.838 --> 00:12:57.870
Well, yeah, it happens, but not to us.

00:12:57.903 --> 00:12:59.104
Look, i could be wrong.

00:12:59.137 --> 00:13:01.471
I'm just saying there's
something about this girl

00:13:01.504 --> 00:13:03.137
That i can't quite put my finger on.

00:13:03.170 --> 00:13:04.804
But i bet you'd like to.

00:13:04.838 --> 00:13:06.504
But maybe she's not a suspect.

00:13:06.537 --> 00:13:08.437
Maybe you got a thing for her, huh?

00:13:08.471 --> 00:13:11.771
You're thinking too much
with your upstairs brain, huh?

00:13:11.804 --> 00:13:13.838
Do me a favor.

00:13:13.870 --> 00:13:17.037
Check and see if there's a
meg masters from massachusetts

00:13:17.070 --> 00:13:19.504
And see if you can't dig
anything up on that symbol.

00:13:19.537 --> 00:13:20.970
What are you gonna do?

00:13:21.003 --> 00:13:22.771
I'm gonna watch meg.

00:13:22.804 --> 00:13:24.204
Yeah.

00:13:24.237 --> 00:13:25.771
I just want to see what's what.

00:13:25.804 --> 00:13:27.304
All right, you little pervert.

00:13:27.337 --> 00:13:29.337
I'm going. I'm going.

00:13:53.504 --> 00:13:54.804
Hey.

00:13:54.838 --> 00:13:56.704
You're lurking outside
that poor girl's apartment,

00:13:56.738 --> 00:13:58.504
Aren't you? No.

00:14:00.037 --> 00:14:01.838
Yes.

00:14:01.870 --> 00:14:03.970
You've got a funny way
of showing your affection.

00:14:04.003 --> 00:14:06.671
You find anything on her or what?

00:14:06.704 --> 00:14:08.671
There's a meg masters in
the andover phone book.

00:14:08.704 --> 00:14:10.704
I even pulled up her high-School photo.

00:14:10.738 --> 00:14:12.870
Now, look, why don't
you go knock on her door

00:14:12.903 --> 00:14:15.204
And invite her to a poetry reading

00:14:15.237 --> 00:14:17.704
Or whatever it is you do, huh?

00:14:17.738 --> 00:14:19.771
What about the symbol? Any luck?

00:14:19.804 --> 00:14:22.070
Yeah, that i did have some luck with.

00:14:22.104 --> 00:14:26.070
Turns out it's zoroastrian.

00:14:26.104 --> 00:14:28.937
Very, very old-School, like
2,000 years before christ.

00:14:28.970 --> 00:14:30.437
It's a sigil for a daeva.

00:14:30.471 --> 00:14:31.903
What's a daeva?

00:14:31.937 --> 00:14:33.903
It translates to
"demon of darkness" --

00:14:33.937 --> 00:14:36.237
Zoroastrian demons, and
they're savage, animalistic,

00:14:36.270 --> 00:14:40.070
Nasty attitudes -- Kind
of like demonic pit bulls.

00:14:40.104 --> 00:14:42.270
How did you figure that out?

00:14:42.304 --> 00:14:44.404
You don't have a corner on
paper chasing around here.

00:14:44.437 --> 00:14:45.870
Name the last book you read.

00:14:47.903 --> 00:14:50.371
I called dad's friend
caleb. He told me, all right.

00:14:50.404 --> 00:14:51.804
Anyway, here's the thing.

00:14:51.838 --> 00:14:54.070
These daevas, they have to be summoned.

00:14:54.104 --> 00:14:55.771
So someone's controlling it?

00:14:55.804 --> 00:14:57.270
Yeah, that's what i'm saying.

00:14:57.304 --> 00:14:59.804
And from what i gather, it's
pretty risky business, too.

00:14:59.838 --> 00:15:02.237
These suckers tend to bite
the hand that feeds them...

00:15:02.270 --> 00:15:04.771
And the arms and the torsos.

00:15:04.804 --> 00:15:05.970
What do they look like?

00:15:06.003 --> 00:15:08.137
Nobody's seen them for
a couple of millennia.

00:15:08.170 --> 00:15:09.771
Summoning a demon that ancient,

00:15:09.804 --> 00:15:11.504
Someone really knows their stuff.

00:15:11.537 --> 00:15:13.371
I think we've got a
major player in town.

00:15:14.838 --> 00:15:17.471
Why don't you go give that
girl a private strip-O-Gram?

00:15:17.504 --> 00:15:19.270
<i>Bite me. Bite her.</i>

00:15:19.304 --> 00:15:21.170
Don't leave teeth marks, though.

00:15:21.204 --> 00:15:23.170
Sam? Are
you --

00:15:52.337 --> 00:15:53.704
No, no,
i'm just --

00:15:53.738 --> 00:15:55.604
Pervert!

00:15:55.637 --> 00:15:58.237
What a creep!

00:18:52.270 --> 00:18:54.571
I don't think you should come

00:18:54.604 --> 00:18:57.404
Because the brothers
-- They're in town.

00:18:57.437 --> 00:18:59.104
I didn't
know that --

00:19:04.237 --> 00:19:05.537
Yes, sir.

00:19:05.571 --> 00:19:11.037
Yes, i'll be here... waiting for you.

00:20:35.337 --> 00:20:38.471
What the hell?

00:20:43.971 --> 00:20:46.603
Dude, i've got to talk to you.

00:20:46.637 --> 00:20:48.804
So, hot little meg is
summoning the daeva?

00:20:48.837 --> 00:20:51.071
It looks like she was
using that black altar

00:20:51.104 --> 00:20:52.404
To control the thing.

00:20:52.438 --> 00:20:54.737
So sammy's got a thing for the bad girl.

00:20:54.770 --> 00:20:56.704
And what's the deal
with that bowl again?

00:20:56.737 --> 00:20:58.537
She was talking
into it --

00:20:58.570 --> 00:21:00.670
The way witches used to
scry into crystal balls.

00:21:00.704 --> 00:21:02.304
She was communicating with someone.

00:21:02.338 --> 00:21:04.971
With the daeva? No, you said
those things were savages.

00:21:05.004 --> 00:21:07.271
No, this was someone different,

00:21:07.304 --> 00:21:09.603
Someone who's giving her orders,

00:21:09.637 --> 00:21:12.371
Someone who's coming to that warehouse.

00:21:21.371 --> 00:21:22.503
Holy crap.

00:21:22.537 --> 00:21:23.971
What?

00:21:24.004 --> 00:21:25.971
What i was gonna tell you earlier.

00:21:26.004 --> 00:21:28.470
I pulled a favor with my

00:21:28.503 --> 00:21:30.937
Friend amy over at
the police department.

00:21:30.971 --> 00:21:33.503
Complete records of the two victims.

00:21:33.537 --> 00:21:35.237
We missed something the first time.

00:21:35.271 --> 00:21:37.904
What?

00:21:37.937 --> 00:21:41.438
The first victim
-- The old man?

00:21:41.470 --> 00:21:43.804
He spent his whole life in chicago,

00:21:43.837 --> 00:21:46.570
But look where he was
born. Lawrence, kansas.

00:21:46.603 --> 00:21:47.904
Mm-Hmm.

00:21:47.937 --> 00:21:49.804
Meredith -- The
second victim?

00:21:49.837 --> 00:21:51.637
It turns out she was adopted.

00:21:51.670 --> 00:21:53.470
And guess where she's from?

00:22:00.837 --> 00:22:01.971
Holy crap.

00:22:02.004 --> 00:22:03.304
Yeah.

00:22:03.338 --> 00:22:05.570
I mean, that is where
the demon killed mom.

00:22:07.304 --> 00:22:08.971
You think meg's tied up with the demon?

00:22:09.004 --> 00:22:11.438
I think it's a definite possibility.

00:22:11.470 --> 00:22:13.971
What's the significance of lawrence?

00:22:14.004 --> 00:22:15.637
And how do these daeva things fit in?

00:22:15.670 --> 00:22:17.971
I say we trash that
black altar, grab meg,

00:22:18.004 --> 00:22:20.737
And have ourselves a
friendly little interrogation.

00:22:20.770 --> 00:22:22.603
No, we can't. We shouldn't tip her off.

00:22:22.637 --> 00:22:24.737
We've got to stake out that warehouse.

00:22:24.770 --> 00:22:27.570
We've got to see who...or
what is showing up to meet her.

00:22:27.603 --> 00:22:28.904
I'll tell you one thing.

00:22:28.937 --> 00:22:31.603
I don't think we should do this alone.

00:22:34.004 --> 00:22:35.470
We think we've got a serious lead

00:22:35.503 --> 00:22:37.137
On the thing that killed mom.

00:22:37.171 --> 00:22:43.304
So, uh, this warehouse
-- It's 1435 west erie.

00:22:43.338 --> 00:22:44.971
Dad, if you get this,

00:22:45.004 --> 00:22:47.837
Get to chicago as soon as you can.

00:22:47.870 --> 00:22:49.503
Voice mail?

00:22:49.537 --> 00:22:50.837
Yeah.

00:22:52.037 --> 00:22:53.503
Jeez. What'd you get?

00:22:53.537 --> 00:22:56.603
I ransacked
that trunk --

00:22:56.637 --> 00:22:59.104
Holy water, y weapon
that i could think of.

00:22:59.137 --> 00:23:02.537
Exorcism rituals from about
a half-Dozen religions.

00:23:02.570 --> 00:23:05.637
I'm not sure what to expect,

00:23:05.670 --> 00:23:08.603
So i guess we should just
expect everything, huh?

00:23:16.704 --> 00:23:19.338
It's a big night.

00:23:19.371 --> 00:23:21.937
Yeah.

00:23:21.971 --> 00:23:23.237
You nervous?

00:23:23.271 --> 00:23:26.770
No. No, are you?

00:23:26.804 --> 00:23:28.971
No. No way.

00:23:37.371 --> 00:23:39.171
God, could you imagine if we actually

00:23:39.204 --> 00:23:40.870
Found that damn thing, that demon?

00:23:40.904 --> 00:23:42.971
Let's not get ahead of
ourselves, all right?

00:23:43.004 --> 00:23:47.770
I know. I'm just
saying... what if we did?

00:23:47.804 --> 00:23:50.804
What if this whole
thing was over tonight?

00:23:50.837 --> 00:23:52.971
Man, i'd sleep for a month,

00:23:53.004 --> 00:23:56.837
Go back to school,
just be a person again.

00:23:56.870 --> 00:23:58.904
You want to go back to school?

00:23:58.937 --> 00:24:01.537
Yeah, once we're done hunting the thing.

00:24:02.704 --> 00:24:05.271
Why? Is there something wrong with that?

00:24:05.304 --> 00:24:09.037
No, no, it's great. Good for you.

00:24:09.071 --> 00:24:12.637
I mean, what are you gonna
do when it's all over?

00:24:12.670 --> 00:24:14.770
It's never gonna be over.

00:24:14.804 --> 00:24:16.071
There's gonna be others.

00:24:16.104 --> 00:24:18.371
There's always gonna
be something to hunt.

00:24:18.404 --> 00:24:21.204
But there's got to be something
that you want for yourself.

00:24:21.237 --> 00:24:23.637
I don't want you to leave
the second this is over.

00:24:23.670 --> 00:24:27.537
Dude, what's your problem?

00:24:33.503 --> 00:24:36.503
Why do you think i drag
you everywhere, huh?

00:24:36.537 --> 00:24:39.737
Why do you think i came
and got you at stanford?

00:24:39.770 --> 00:24:42.004
'Cause dad was in trouble.

00:24:42.037 --> 00:24:44.670
'Cause you wanted to find
the thing that killed mom.

00:24:44.704 --> 00:24:46.837
Yes, that, but it's more than that, man.

00:24:53.371 --> 00:24:58.004
You and me
and dad --

00:24:58.037 --> 00:25:01.404
I want us to be together again.

00:25:03.371 --> 00:25:07.670
I want us to be a family again.

00:25:07.704 --> 00:25:12.371
<i>Dean, we are a family.
I'd do anything for you.</i>

00:25:12.404 --> 00:25:15.404
But things will never be
the way they were before.

00:25:21.004 --> 00:25:23.670
They could be.

00:25:27.371 --> 00:25:29.037
I don't want them to be.

00:25:33.204 --> 00:25:35.204
I'm not gonna live this life forever.

00:25:35.237 --> 00:25:38.570
Dean, when this is all over,

00:25:38.603 --> 00:25:41.837
You're gonna have to
let me go my own way.

00:26:44.603 --> 00:26:48.870
Guys. Hiding is a little bit
childish, don't you think?

00:26:48.904 --> 00:26:50.870
That didn't work out like i'd planned.

00:26:53.804 --> 00:26:53.904
Why don't you come out?

00:27:04.071 --> 00:27:07.570
Sam, i have to say,

00:27:07.603 --> 00:27:10.304
This puts a real crimp
in our relationship.

00:27:10.338 --> 00:27:12.171
Yeah, tell me about it.

00:27:12.204 --> 00:27:14.870
So, where's your little daeva friend?

00:27:14.904 --> 00:27:16.104
Around.

00:27:16.137 --> 00:27:18.770
And that shotgun's
not gonna do much good.

00:27:18.804 --> 00:27:20.704
Oh, don't worry, sweetheart.

00:27:20.737 --> 00:27:22.237
The shotgun's not for the demon.

00:27:22.271 --> 00:27:25.837
So, who is it, meg? Who's coming?

00:27:25.870 --> 00:27:27.338
Who are you waiting for?

00:27:27.371 --> 00:27:29.870
You.

00:28:00.121 --> 00:28:03.287
Hey, sam, don't take this the wrong way,

00:28:03.321 --> 00:28:06.653
But your girlfriend... is a bitch.

00:28:06.687 --> 00:28:10.854
This, the whole thing, was a trap.

00:28:12.753 --> 00:28:15.387
Running into you at the bar,

00:28:15.421 --> 00:28:19.121
Following you here, hearing
what you had to say --

00:28:19.154 --> 00:28:21.187
It was all a setup, wasn't it?

00:28:22.787 --> 00:28:24.787
And that the victims were from lawrence.

00:28:24.820 --> 00:28:26.187
It doesn't mean anything.

00:28:26.221 --> 00:28:28.820
It was just to draw you in, that's all.

00:28:28.854 --> 00:28:30.687
You killed those two people for nothing.

00:28:30.720 --> 00:28:32.987
Baby, i've killed a
lot more for a lot less.

00:28:34.887 --> 00:28:38.020
You trapped us. Good for you.

00:28:38.054 --> 00:28:40.354
It's miller time.

00:28:40.387 --> 00:28:42.187
Why don't you kill us already?

00:28:42.221 --> 00:28:45.321
Not very quick on the uptake, are we?

00:28:50.954 --> 00:28:52.620
This trap isn't for you.

00:28:56.488 --> 00:28:57.653
Dad.

00:28:58.820 --> 00:29:00.254
It's a trap for dad.

00:29:03.121 --> 00:29:05.954
Oh, sweetheart, you're
dumber than you look.

00:29:05.987 --> 00:29:09.920
'Cause even if dad was
in town, which he is not,

00:29:09.954 --> 00:29:11.920
He wouldn't walk into
something like this.

00:29:11.954 --> 00:29:13.653
He's too good.

00:29:13.687 --> 00:29:16.020
He is pretty good, i'll give you that.

00:29:21.020 --> 00:29:23.020
But you see

00:29:28.354 --> 00:29:30.154
He has one weakness.

00:29:30.187 --> 00:29:31.521
What's that?

00:29:31.554 --> 00:29:33.287
You.

00:29:34.687 --> 00:29:37.554
He lets his guard down around his boys,

00:29:37.588 --> 00:29:40.954
Lets his emotions cloud his judgment.

00:29:42.920 --> 00:29:45.720
<i>I happen to know he is in town,</i>

00:29:45.753 --> 00:29:50.488
And he'll come and try to save you.

00:29:50.521 --> 00:29:53.387
And then the daevas
will kill everybody --

00:29:53.421 --> 00:29:57.987
Nice and slow... and messy.

00:29:58.020 --> 00:30:00.321
Well, i've got news for you.

00:30:00.354 --> 00:30:03.653
It's gonna take a lot more
than some...shadow to kill him.

00:30:03.687 --> 00:30:05.854
Oh, the daevas are in the room here.

00:30:05.887 --> 00:30:07.087
They're invisible.

00:30:07.121 --> 00:30:09.454
Their shadows are just
the only part you can see.

00:30:09.488 --> 00:30:10.987
Why are you doing this, meg?

00:30:11.020 --> 00:30:13.221
What kind of deal you got
worked out here, huh...

00:30:13.254 --> 00:30:14.554
And with who?

00:30:14.588 --> 00:30:16.488
I'm doing this for the same reasons

00:30:16.521 --> 00:30:18.488
You do what
you do --

00:30:18.521 --> 00:30:20.854
Loyalty, love.

00:30:26.521 --> 00:30:28.488
Like the love you had for
mommy...and jess.Go to he

00:30:28.521 --> 00:30:32.054
Baby, i'm already there.

00:30:34.087 --> 00:30:36.221
Come on, sam.

00:30:36.254 --> 00:30:39.254
There's no need to be nasty.

00:30:43.753 --> 00:30:47.720
I think we both know...

00:30:47.753 --> 00:30:50.588
How you really feel about me.

00:30:54.020 --> 00:30:55.687
You know

00:30:57.753 --> 00:31:01.720
I saw you... watching me...

00:31:01.753 --> 00:31:05.287
Changing in my apartment.

00:31:05.321 --> 00:31:07.887
It turned you on, didn't it?

00:31:07.920 --> 00:31:09.920
Get a room, you two.

00:31:09.954 --> 00:31:11.454
I didn't mind.

00:31:11.488 --> 00:31:14.121
I liked that you were watching me.

00:31:14.154 --> 00:31:16.121
Come on, sammy,

00:31:16.154 --> 00:31:19.121
You and i can still
have a little dirty fun.

00:31:19.154 --> 00:31:21.753
You want to have fun? Go ahead, then.

00:31:21.787 --> 00:31:24.287
I'm a little tied up right now.

00:31:59.488 --> 00:32:02.454
Now, were you just trying to distract me

00:32:02.488 --> 00:32:05.620
While your brother cuts free?

00:32:05.653 --> 00:32:08.287
No.

00:32:08.321 --> 00:32:10.287
No.

00:32:10.321 --> 00:32:13.187
It was because i have a knife of my own.

00:32:15.887 --> 00:32:17.187
Sam!

00:32:17.221 --> 00:32:19.054
Get the altar.

00:32:58.720 --> 00:33:00.354
So, i guess the daevas

00:33:00.388 --> 00:33:02.687
Didn't like being bossed around.

00:33:02.720 --> 00:33:04.854
I guess not.

00:33:04.887 --> 00:33:06.187
Hey, sam?

00:33:06.221 --> 00:33:07.354
Hmm?

00:33:07.388 --> 00:33:09.354
Next time you want to get laid,

00:33:09.388 --> 00:33:13.054
Find a girl that's not
so buckets of crazy, huh?

00:33:27.854 --> 00:33:30.254
Why don't you just leave
that stuff in the car?

00:33:30.288 --> 00:33:32.587
I said it before, and
i'll say it again --

00:33:32.620 --> 00:33:35.787
Better safe than sorry.

00:33:39.354 --> 00:33:40.520
Hey!

00:33:53.420 --> 00:33:55.021
Dad.

00:33:55.054 --> 00:33:57.054
Hey, boys.

00:34:25.420 --> 00:34:26.553
Hi, sam.

00:34:26.587 --> 00:34:27.921
Hi, dad.

00:34:31.453 --> 00:34:33.754
Dad, it was a trap.

00:34:33.787 --> 00:34:37.420
I didn't know. I'm sorry.

00:34:37.453 --> 00:34:40.553
It's all right. I thought
it might have been.

00:34:40.587 --> 00:34:42.121
Were you there?

00:34:42.154 --> 00:34:46.487
I got there just in time to
see the girl take the swan dive.

00:34:46.520 --> 00:34:47.887
She was the bad guy, right?

00:34:47.921 --> 00:34:49.420
Yes, sir.Yes, sir.

00:34:49.453 --> 00:34:51.921
Good. Well, it doesn't surprise me.

00:34:51.954 --> 00:34:54.388
It's tried to stop me before.

00:34:54.453 --> 00:34:56.420
The demon has?

00:34:56.453 --> 00:34:59.754
It knows i'm close. It
knows i'm gonna kill it.

00:34:59.787 --> 00:35:03.354
Not just exorcise it
or send it back to hell,

00:35:03.388 --> 00:35:06.154
Actually kill it.

00:35:06.187 --> 00:35:07.754
How?

00:35:07.787 --> 00:35:10.854
I'm working on that.

00:35:10.887 --> 00:35:14.520
Let us come with you. We'll help.

00:35:14.553 --> 00:35:18.121
No, sam.

00:35:18.154 --> 00:35:19.187
Not yet.

00:35:19.221 --> 00:35:21.453
Listen, try to understand.

00:35:21.487 --> 00:35:23.921
This demon is a scary son of a bitch.

00:35:23.954 --> 00:35:26.587
I don't want you
caught in the crossfire.

00:35:26.620 --> 00:35:27.921
I don't want you hurt.

00:35:27.954 --> 00:35:30.087
You don't have to worry about us.

00:35:30.121 --> 00:35:31.121
Of course i do.

00:35:33.453 --> 00:35:35.453
I'm your father.

00:35:39.487 --> 00:35:43.787
Listen, sammy, the last
time we were together,

00:35:43.820 --> 00:35:45.620
We had one hell of a fight.

00:35:45.654 --> 00:35:46.787
Yes, sir.

00:35:54.654 --> 00:35:57.620
It's good to see you again.

00:35:57.654 --> 00:35:59.487
It's been a long time.

00:36:01.887 --> 00:36:03.221
Too long.

00:36:30.720 --> 00:36:32.221
No!

00:37:10.967 --> 00:37:12.834
These things are shadow demons,

00:37:12.867 --> 00:37:14.567
So let's light 'em up!

00:37:29.533 --> 00:37:30.667
Dad!

00:37:30.700 --> 00:37:31.901
Over here!

00:37:34.101 --> 00:37:36.334
Come on!

00:38:01.167 --> 00:38:03.467
All right, come on. We
don't have much time.

00:38:03.500 --> 00:38:05.967
As soon as the flare's
out, they'll be back.

00:38:06.001 --> 00:38:07.533
Wait, wait!

00:38:07.567 --> 00:38:09.934
Sam, wait.

00:38:13.567 --> 00:38:15.034
Dad, you can't come with us.

00:38:15.067 --> 00:38:20.268
What? What are you talking about?

00:38:20.301 --> 00:38:21.800
We'll be all right.

00:38:21.834 --> 00:38:24.600
Dean, we should stick together!
We'll go after those --

00:38:24.634 --> 00:38:25.967
Sam, listen to me!

00:38:28.901 --> 00:38:30.934
We almost got dad killed in there.

00:38:30.967 --> 00:38:33.934
Don't you understand?
They're not gonna stop.

00:38:33.967 --> 00:38:35.533
They're gonna try again.

00:38:35.567 --> 00:38:37.967
They're gonna use us to get to him.

00:38:38.001 --> 00:38:39.667
I mean, meg was right.

00:38:39.700 --> 00:38:42.500
Dad's vulnerable when he's with us.

00:38:44.101 --> 00:38:48.500
He...he's stronger without us around.

00:38:50.567 --> 00:38:52.234
Dad...

00:38:53.934 --> 00:38:55.901
No.

00:38:55.934 --> 00:38:58.034
After everything,

00:38:58.067 --> 00:39:00.800
After all the time we
spent looking for you,

00:39:00.834 --> 00:39:03.334
Please.

00:39:03.368 --> 00:39:05.101
I've got to be a part of this fight.

00:39:05.134 --> 00:39:07.101
Sammy, this fight is just starting,

00:39:07.134 --> 00:39:09.834
And we are all gonna
have a part to play.

00:39:09.867 --> 00:39:11.600
For now, you've got to trust me, son.

00:39:13.967 --> 00:39:17.901
Okay? You've got to let me go.

00:40:01.734 --> 00:40:03.867
Be careful, boys.

00:40:05.167 --> 00:40:07.001
Come on.



00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:10.000
